// CHUNK 05 -- THE CONTRACT-EPOCH REAL-EXECUTION WITNESSES. Each builds a real temporary
// repository and commits into it, so each reaches shell.Mktemp.Dir, which declares no
// mock_response. The subject cannot be reached any other way: the discriminating experiment is
// TWO COMMITS whose trees differ only in the contract-epoch member, so a fixture that constructed
// the observation instead would assert the fold's arithmetic while proving nothing about the
// reader that produces it. The remedy is the route, not a weaker assertion.
//
// THE SENTENCE THAT STOOD HERE SAID THESE FOUR "RUN GREEN TODAY IN THE WET BIN LANE", AND IT WAS
// FALSE WHEN IT WAS WRITTEN. BinWitnessWet's scheduler, falsifier.yml, was deleted at 611fd02770
// on 2026-08-15; enrolment by entry and function name is not execution, and these four executed
// nowhere. The required floor said so on this branch: standing=planned-without-terminal-verdict,
// outcome=route-gap-before-verdict, with failed=0 and unexpected_failures=0. That is the same
// enrolled-reads-as-covered class this module exists to type, reproduced by a note about it.
//
// These rows STAY, and they are not the thing that changed. They are the truthful HERMETIC
// observation: the identity executed, reached shell.Mktemp.Dir, which declares no mock_response,
// and was counted and held. What discharges the hold is a candidate-bound wet terminal from
// v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal, whose schedule now carries these four -- each measured wet
// before being scheduled. Held plus a same-identity, same-candidate wet pass is the joined
// standing; the hold is never read as a pass on its own.
