// THE STEP 0 CALIBRATION REPORT'S WET EVIDENCE, enrolled on the same basis as chunk_05 above and
// measured the same way. Required-floor run 33978797098 at 06c7740cb1 executed all four
// identities and observed the identical typed refusal for each: the hermetic route has no arm for
// Dir, because shell.Mktemp.Dir declares no mock_response, so the claim refuses before a temporary
// directory can exist. The operation and ground below are READ FROM THAT RUN, not inferred -- the
// enrollment was deliberately withheld until the measurement existed, because a roster row written
// from a guess is a transcribed number wearing a data row's clothes.
//
// WHAT DISCHARGES THE HOLD IS THE WET TERMINAL, NEVER THE ENROLLMENT. The same run recorded
// [local-repo-wet] scheduled=22 admitted=22 refusals=0 with all four of these observed=passed, and
// the changed-witness projection then read standing=hermetic-route-gap-held-and-wet-passed for
// each. Enrollment alone would record a gap and prove nothing; the pair is what establishes that
// the witness reached its subject somewhere.
//
// WHY THE WITNESS CANNOT BE MADE HERMETIC, stated because the diagnostic offers mocking as one of
// its three remedies and it is the wrong one HERE. These four exist to prove that the REAL report
// writes the REAL matrix to a REAL path before it refuses -- the defect they were written against
// was a write arm that accepted a zero-byte file. A mocked Dir and a mocked Write would satisfy
// every assertion while the operator still received nothing, which is the fabricated-plausible-
// output failure the witnesses exist to catch. The route is supplied by the wet lane instead.
//
// THE ENROLLMENT IS NOT A PAIR BUT A TRIPLE, AND NOTHING ENFORCES IT; THIS PARAGRAPH IS PROSE,
// WHICH CANNOT REFUSE. THREE ROWS ARE REQUIRED, IN THREE SEPARATE AUTHORITIES, AND NONE OF THEM
// REFERENCES THE OTHERS: the expectation here in v2.workflow.floor_route_gap
// floor_route_gap_expectation_chunk_06; the schedule row in
// v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal local_repo_wet_schedule; and the
// gunbc.ci_layer_roots witness_exclusion_frontier row classifying the file LocalRepoWetLane.
// NOTHING REFUSES A WITNESS THAT HAS SOME OF THE THREE AND NOT ALL. That is stated as a declared
// boundary rather than as advice: the reader is being told what this text cannot do for them.
// The carriers are named by SYMBOL and not by line, because a citation that decays under the next
// edit above it is the failure this roster already carries a row for.
//
// AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS PARAGRAPH SAID "PAIR" AND NAMED TWO OF THE THREE. It was written to
// be the honest statement of the coupling and it understated the coupling, which is worse than
// silence here: an author following it supplies two of three, gets a red floor, and is misled by
// the sentence meant to save them -- and it will be TRUSTED, because it is a declared boundary in
// the file they are already editing. It was caught by a reviewer counting the carriers, not by
// its author, who had checked a DIFFERENT count in this same change an hour earlier and did not
// check this one.
//
// THE EVIDENCE THAT PROSE CANNOT CARRY THIS IS THIS REPOSITORY'S OWN HISTORY, TWICE IN ONE DAY.
// floor_prepared_subject_exclusions carries a comment reading "run_required_floor consults THIS
// list and nothing else", written by an author who had just spent three CI cycles learning it; it
// did not reach the next author, who spent more. chunk_05's header above states this same pairing
// in this same file, and it did not reach the author of chunk_06, who supplied the schedule row
// alone and learned the rest from five red floors. A comment is read by whoever already knew to
// look for it.
//
// AND THE ONE WALL GUARDING THESE ROWS CANNOT FIRE FOR THE POPULATION THAT NEEDS IT.
// floor_route_gap_expectation_mismatch refuses a WRONG operation or ground, but it returns early
// on a missing expectation, so it fires only for an identity that is ALREADY ENROLLED. An
// unenrolled identity -- the state every author is in while deciding what to write here --
// produces no mismatch diagnostic at all and blocks as an unenrolled gap with nothing said about
// what the right row would have been. A guard whose precondition is the state you are not yet in
