// THE DECLARED-UNIT DIGEST MINT IS THE ONE ROUTE GAP THESE IDENTITIES SHARE.
// gunbc.spark.pair_serving_realization spark_pair_rendered_unit_digest calls
// extdeps.tools.sha256sum Sha256.DigestStdin, which declares no mock_response, so the hermetic
// floor has no route that can run it. DeclaredUnitDigestEvidence is a sole_constructor record, so
// no fixture can route around that by authoring a standing -- which is the point rather than a
// cost: every identity below executes the REAL producer on the local-repo wet lane
// (v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal local_repo_wet_schedule), which is the inhabitance half of
// DESIGN section 3's supplied-input pairing obligation.
//
// WHAT DECIDES MEMBERSHIP HERE IS WHETHER THE ROW REACHES THE MINT, NOT WHICH ARM THE FOLD ANSWERS
// ON. An earlier spelling of this paragraph said the declared-unit-unavailable rows are omitted
// "because the arm is decided before the mint is reached", and that is FALSE as a rule and misread
// once already (review 67105 asked for a correct enrollment to be deleted on the strength of it).
// The fold's refusal order says nothing about what the row EVALUATED to build its arguments: a row
// can hand in DeclaredUnitDigestUnavailable and still reach DigestStdin through its INCARNATION
// fixture, because that launch's unit_digest is taken from the production mint so the agreeing and
// disagreeing arms compare real bytes.
//
// THE TWO t_unit_unavailable ROWS ARE EXACTLY THAT CONTRAST, and they are the reason to state this
// precisely rather than by arm name:
//   an_observed_incarnation_without_a_declared_unit_digest_refuses -- supplies the unavailable
//     standing AND an observed incarnation built from t_incarnation(), which routes through
//     t_declared_digest() to spark_pair_declared_head_digest. It gaps. ENROLLED.
//   the_declared_unit_is_refused_before_the_incarnation -- supplies the unavailable standing over a
//     bare t_covered_matching() with no incarnation fixture. It never reaches the mint. OMITTED.
// Read the row's whole argument closure, not the arm it asserts.
//
// The withdrawn-roster row in the bind witness is omitted for the different reason that it is HANDED
// its standing and constructs no launch fixture.
fn floor_route_gap_expectation_chunk_14() -> List<FloorRouteGapExpectation> {
  Cons {
    head: FloorRouteGapExpectation { identity: "test.claim.spark.spark_pair_head_unit_digest_witness.hashing_the_same_rendered_bytes_is_stable", operation: "DigestStdin", ground: NoMockResponse {} },
    tail: Cons {
      head: FloorRouteGapExpectation { identity: "test.claim.spark.spark_pair_head_unit_digest_witness.unit_text_differing_by_one_byte_gives_a_different_digest", operation: "DigestStdin", ground: NoMockResponse {} },
      tail: Cons {
        head: FloorRouteGapExpectation { identity: "test.claim.spark.spark_pair_head_unit_digest_witness.spark_pair_head_unit_declared_digest_hashes_the_realized_head_unit", operation: "DigestStdin", ground: NoMockResponse {} },
        tail: Cons {
          head: FloorRouteGapExpectation { identity: "test.claim.serving.serving_availability_bind_wet_witness.the_production_roster_carries_the_declared_digest_to_the_incarnation_frontier", operation: "DigestStdin", ground: NoMockResponse {} },
